# serializer version: 1
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac --help]
  '''
  $ maniac --help
  [exit 0]
  
   Usage: maniac [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...
  
   Manpages for the tools you install, kept matching their versions: the page a tool ships, else its project's, else one
   an LLM writes from its --help.
  
  ╭─ Options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ --verbose             -v        Also print diagnostic detail as maniac works. [env var: MANIAC_VERBOSE]              │
  │ --install-completion            Install completion for the current shell.                                            │
  │ --show-completion               Show completion for the current shell, to copy it or customize the installation.     │
  │ --help                          Show this message and exit.                                                          │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  ╭─ Commands ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ install  Install a page for each tool: shipped, else upstream, else generated.                                       │
  │ update   Reinstall each page maniac installed whose tool changed version.                                            │
  │ remove   Remove the pages maniac installed, and restore any page each replaced.                                      │
  │ list     The pages maniac installed: the version each documents, the version installed.                              │
  │ scan     Your other tools and their pages, found across your login $PATH.                                            │
  │ why      Explain every decision maniac makes about a tool, and what `install` would do.                              │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac install --help]
  '''
  $ maniac install --help
  [exit 0]
  
   Usage: maniac install [OPTIONS] [tools]...
  
   Install a page for each tool: shipped, else upstream, else generated.
  
   Shipped is the page the tool installed itself; upstream, its project's
   page for the installed version; generated, one an LLM writes from its
   --help and its project's docs.
  
   A page already current is left alone. With no tools it does nothing, so
   `maniac scan --available | xargs maniac install` is safe when the list
   is empty.
  
  ╭─ Arguments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │   tools      <str>  Tools to install pages for.                                                                      │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  ╭─ Options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ --model                <str>  LLM model ID (e.g. 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash').                                         │
  │ --no-generate                 Use only a shipped or upstream page; never call an LLM.                                │
  │ --force        -f             Install where maniac would refuse: over a page it did not install (kept as a backup),  │
  │                               for a tool installed only in this project, or for a system package's tool. Also        │
  │                               reinstalls a page already current.                                                     │
  │ --dry-run                     Preview without installing or generating anything.                                     │
  │ --help                        Show this message and exit.                                                            │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac install cowsay --no-generate]
  '''
  $ maniac install cowsay --no-generate
  [exit 1]
  cowsay   not installed: the check for an upstream page in piuccio/cowsay did not complete (network or git?), so whether one exists is unknown; rerun once it can
    documents <npm>/bin/cowsay (npm, 1.6.0)
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac install faketool marked cowsay]
  '''
  $ maniac install faketool marked cowsay
  [exit 1]
  faketool   installed: generated page, from --help (3 commands)
    documents <tmp>/bin/faketool (no installer; it reports faketool 2.3.1)
  
  marked   installed: shipped page (16.4.2)
    documents <npm>/bin/marked (npm, 16.4.2)
  
  cowsay   not installed: Could not confirm whether piuccio/cowsay has a manpage for 'cowsay' -- the tier-2 repository check failed rather than returning a definitive answer, so synthesizing over it could silently paper over a network or git failure. Rerun once the check can complete; `maniac why cowsay` shows what was tried.
  
  1 of 3 not installed.
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac install marked (already current)]
  '''
  $ maniac install marked
  [exit 0]
  marked   already up to date (16.4.2); --force reinstalls it
    documents <npm>/bin/marked (npm, 16.4.2)
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac install marked --dry-run --force]
  '''
  $ maniac install marked --dry-run --force
  [exit 0]
  marked   would install: shipped page (16.4.2)
    documents <npm>/bin/marked (npm, 16.4.2)
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac install nowhere-xyz]
  '''
  $ maniac install nowhere-xyz
  [exit 1]
  nowhere-xyz   not installed: 'nowhere-xyz' is not on your login shell's $PATH -- and a manpage would be installed globally and permanently. Install it globally first, or make your login profile put it on $PATH.
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac install]
  '''
  $ maniac install
  [exit 0]
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac list (terminal) (after remove)]
  '''
