# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac list --help]
  '''
  $ maniac list --help
  [exit 0]
  
   Usage: maniac list [OPTIONS] [tools]...
  
   The pages maniac installed: the version each documents, the version installed.
  
   `scan` shows your other tools.
  
  ╭─ Arguments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │   tools      <str>  Tools to show. With none, every page maniac installed.                                           │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  ╭─ Options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ --names             Bare tool names, one per line, even on a terminal.                                               │
  │ --outdated          Only pages that document another version.                                                        │
  │ --unknown           Only pages whose version nothing proves either way.                                              │
  │ --help              Show this message and exit.                                                                      │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac list cowsay faketool]
  '''
  $ maniac list cowsay faketool
  [exit 1]
  faketool
  cowsay   maniac installed no page for it; `maniac scan cowsay` shows its state.
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac list]
  '''
  $ maniac list
  [exit 0]
  faketool
  marked
  
  '''
