# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac update --help]
  '''
  $ maniac update --help
  [exit 0]
  
   Usage: maniac update [OPTIONS] [tools]...
  
   Reinstall each page maniac installed whose tool changed version.
  
   Only `outdated` pages: one whose version is `unknown` is left alone until
   you name it to `maniac install`. Each tool commits on its own, so an
   interrupted update resumes by running it again.
  
  ╭─ Arguments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │   tools      <str>  Pages to update. With none, every outdated page maniac installed.                                │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  ╭─ Options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ --model              <str>  LLM model ID (e.g. 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash').                                           │
  │ --no-generate               Use only a shipped or upstream page; never call an LLM.                                  │
  │ --dry-run                   Preview without installing or generating anything.                                       │
  │ --help                      Show this message and exit.                                                              │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac update marked cowsay]
  '''
  $ maniac update marked cowsay
  [exit 1]
  cowsay   maniac installed no page for it.
  marked   up to date
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac update]
  '''
  $ maniac update
  [exit 0]
  Every page maniac installed is up to date.
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac why --help]
  '''
  $ maniac why --help
  [exit 0]
  
   Usage: maniac why [OPTIONS] {tool}
  
   Explain every decision maniac makes about a tool, and what `install` would do.
  
  ╭─ Arguments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ *    tool      <str>  The tool to explain. [required]                                                                │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  ╭─ Options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ --help-text          Also print the --help output a generated page would be written from.                            │
  │ --docs               Also list the repository documents a generated page would use.                                  │
  │ --help               Show this message and exit.                                                                     │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac why cowsay]
  '''
  $ maniac why cowsay
  [exit 0]
  PATH     read from `/bin/sh -lc` started in $HOME: <n> directories
           <n> more this shell has are left out; none holds this tool
  Binary   login $PATH reaches <npm>/bin/cowsay
           installed by npm as cowsay (1.6.0), root <npm>/lib/node_modules/cowsay
  Page     `man` finds no page for it
  Sources  shipped: none in <npm>/lib/node_modules/cowsay
           upstream: piuccio/cowsay at 1.6.0: the check failed (network?), so install refuses to generate
           generated: from its own --help (`why --help-text`) and piuccio/cowsay's docs (`why --docs`)
  install  refused: the upstream check did not complete
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac why faketool]
  '''
  $ maniac why faketool
  [exit 0]
  PATH     read from `/bin/sh -lc` started in $HOME: <n> directories
           <n> more this shell has are left out; none holds this tool
  Binary   login $PATH reaches <tmp>/bin/faketool
           no installer claims it; it reports faketool 2.3.1
  Page     maniac's (generated): documents faketool 2.3.1, installed faketool 2.3.1: ok
  Sources  shipped: no installer, so no install root to look in
           upstream: no installer, so no repository or version known
           generated: from its own --help (`why --help-text` shows it)
  install  already up to date (faketool 2.3.1); --force reinstalls it (generated)
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac why marked]
  '''
  $ maniac why marked
  [exit 0]
  PATH     read from `/bin/sh -lc` started in $HOME: <n> directories
           <n> more this shell has are left out; none holds this tool
  Binary   login $PATH reaches <npm>/bin/marked
           installed by npm as marked (16.4.2), root <npm>/lib/node_modules/marked
  Page     maniac's (shipped): documents 16.4.2, installed 16.4.2: ok
  Sources  shipped: <npm>/lib/node_modules/marked/man/marked.1
  install  already up to date (16.4.2); --force reinstalls it (shipped)
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_every_command_as_a_user_sees_it[maniac why nowhere-xyz]
  '''
  $ maniac why nowhere-xyz
  [exit 0]
  PATH     read from `/bin/sh -lc` started in $HOME: <n> directories
           <n> more this shell has are left out; none holds this tool
